        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505312.189061
      },
      "rev_n_3_d7e295_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_d7e295_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_d7e295",
        "thought_text": "Iterate over possible values of D starting from 0 and check if the conditions are met by building roads up to that distance.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505312.189069
      },
      "rev_n_2_5296a1_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_5296a1_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_5296a1",
        "thought_text": "Use binary search to efficiently find the minimal \\( D \\) such that there exists a county where the sum of residents in any subset is divisible by \\( K \\). This approach ensures that we can quickly narrow down the possible values of \\( D \\) without having to check every possible distance manually.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_5296a1_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_c6b6c8772c",
        "created_at": 1794505357.2020311
      },
      "rev_n_3_d7e295_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_d7e295_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_d7e295",
        "thought_text": "Iterate over possible values of D starting from 0 and incrementally increase D until the conditions are met by building roads up to that distance. This approach ensures that we find the minimal D efficiently while checking the required conditions.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_d7e295_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_fe82494a7b",
        "created_at": 1794505391.7578936
      },
      "rev_n_4_b388fa_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_b388fa_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_b388fa",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the MST for each possible value of D and check if any county has a subset of cities with a sum of residents divisible by K.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "91686312714609859",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505411.7606173
      },
      "rev_n_5_a1ca35_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_a1ca35_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_a1ca35",
        "thought_text": "Use dynamic programming to keep track of the sums of residents modulo K for subsets of cities reachable within each radius D.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "91686312714609859",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505411.7606325
      },
      "rev_n_6_ed5dd2_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_ed5dd2_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_ed5dd2",
        "thought_text": "Employ a union-find data structure to efficiently manage and merge counties while checking for the required subset condition.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "91686312714609859",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505411.7606418
      },
      "rev_n_5_a1ca35_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_a1ca35_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_a1ca35",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Instead of directly attempting to calculate the MST for every possible diameter, use binary search on the diameter. For each midpoint value during the binary search, check if there exists a valid MST where the sum of residents in at least one county is divisible by K. This approach ensures that we efficiently narrow down the optimal diameter without unnecessary calculations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "91686312714609859",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_a1ca35_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_158abbbdd1",
        "created_at": 1794505433.1878145
      },
      "rev_n_4_b388fa_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_b388fa_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_b388fa",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Instead of calculating the MST for each possible value of D, use a binary search approach to find the minimal D. For each midpoint D in the binary search, calculate the MST and check if any county has a subset of cities with a sum of residents divisible by K. If such a subset exists, update the upper bound; otherwise, update the lower bound. This approach ensures that we efficiently narrow down the possible values of D without recalculating the MST from scratch for each candidate D.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "91686312714609859",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_b388fa_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ced5cab05d",
        "created_at": 1794505469.221468
      },
      "rev_n_6_ed5dd2_1": {
